Japanese:
宿の主人
「すいません、お金が足りません
　よ」{END}

English:
Innkeeper
 I'm sorry, but you don't have
 enough money.{END}

Japanese:
町の人
「マーテル様、どうか世界をお守
　り下さい・・・」{END}

English:
Citizen
 Lady Martel, please protect the
 world...{END}

Japanese:
練習生
「道場が狭いので、外で練習して
　います」{END}

町の人
「ここら辺りは、魔物も少なくて
　助かります」{END}

English:
Citizen
 This region's relatively safe with so
 few monsters roaming about.{END}

Japanese:
師範
「最近、何か練習生の数が増えて
　きたな」{END}

English:
Instructor
 There's been a sudden influx
 of new students lately.{END}

Old Man
 Oh, it's you.
 Was that book helpful?{END}

Old Man
 It wasn't because I overworked
 myself...{END}

Boy
 Tag!
 YOU'RE IT!{END}

Japanese:
魔術師
「それって、どんなすごいものな
　んだろうね・・・」{END}

English:
Mage
 Forbidden magic must really be
 something else...{END}

Japanese:
ローブを着た人
「収集品を集めるためには、交換
　が重要よ」{END}

English:
Robed Woman
 Trading with other collectors is key
 to completing one's own collection.{END}

Robed Woman
 To get you started,
 I'll give you this.<wait>{END}

Japanese:
ローブを着た人
「今後のために、聞いておいたほ
　うが、いいと思うけど・・・」{END}

English:
Robed Woman
 Oh? Not into trendy stuff, huh?
 Ah well...{END}

Chef
 What!?
 How can you reject this taste!?{END}
